    "_comment_deny": "Deny what no verdict is ever derived from (ADR-20260816-020752, farley): build output and object stores are re-derivable from source, so reading them costs tokens and can never change a gate result. Mirrors .claudeignore -- keep the two in step. DELIBERATELY NOT DENIED: specs/generated/** (the drift gate's evidence; denying it makes check-drift unauditable), Cargo.lock (a lock diff is a supply-chain review), tools/codegen-rs/warning-baseline.json (the warning ratchet). Also here: honeycomb is DISABLED above, not deleted -- unauthenticated its tools cannot run and no runtime emits spans yet; RE-AUTH IS THE EVENT THAT RE-ENABLES IT (delete the entry). The .mcp.json definition stays so the eu1 EU-host pin (a GDPR constraint) is not lost with the server config.",
